{"number":1499,"title":"A session that cannot run converge-item.mjs improvises its converge — three divergent outcomes observed","body":"MCP-only sessions (no `api.github.com`) cannot run `converge-item.mjs`, and the verify-in-production playbook and the queue&#39;s converge rules don&#39;t say what such a session should do instead. Three different improvisations shipped: #1316 closed per the VIP playbook (correct); #1265 and #1220 hand-set a `task:done` **label** without closing — the pass is recorded nowhere the queue reads, and the done label hides them from the leash, so nothing ever comes back; #1260/#1268/#1288/#1291 were left untouched.

Wanted: one documented MCP-only converge path (Shepherd&#39;s local pack already carries the manual replication recipe) — or route ad-hoc verification runs through the Action-side executor only.

