{"number":1500,"title":"verify-in-production files checks the runner environment cannot read","body":"Verifications get filed whose `Verify:` names an artifact the unattended runner structurally cannot observe: `*.github.io` pages sit behind the egress block (#1184, #1288, #1253) and cross-repo reads behind MCP scope (#1268, #1291). In one executor batch (2026-08-24), 5 of 7 claimed items parked on these environment limits — each burning a session to rediscover the same wall, then degrading into a `needs-human` park, which is the human-memory outcome the skill exists to avoid. The opposite miss also occurred: #1460 was hand-verified 12 minutes after filing, so it was watchable in-session and shouldn&#39;t have been filed at all.

Skill amendment wanted: before filing, test `Verify:` against what the runner can actually reach — file the explicit human-step form when it can&#39;t, and file nothing when the artifact is readable now.

